/// Chapter 40 of the guide, written from md-docs/reference/glossary.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page GlossaryGuide(path: "/reference/glossary", title: "Glossary", description: "The terms this guide uses — state, signal, pre-rendered page, hydration, flag, part, slot, registry, scope and more — each in a sentence, with a link.", layout: DocsShell("Glossary", kind: .reference, chapter: t("nav.group.reference"), blurb: "The words this guide uses, each in a sentence, with where to read more.", source: "md-docs/reference/glossary.md", sections: [], prevTo: "/reference/browser-support", prevLabel: t("ch.39"), nextTo: "/reference/library", nextLabel: t("ch.41"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This glossary defines the words this guide uses, in alphabetical order. Each entry is one sentence, with a link to the chapter that explains the idea. The guide uses each term in the same sense every time.\n\n**Action.** A named function of a page, component or store whose body changes state or does other work: `action add() \{ … \}` ([State and reactivity](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#actions-and-locals)).\n\n**App shell.** The `app \{ \}` declaration: what every page is drawn inside, with a `Router` where the current page goes ([Pages and routing](/learn/05-pages-and-routing#the-app-shell)).\n\n**Block.** The `\{ … \}` after an element, holding its style, transitions, handlers, slot fills and children, in that order ([Elements](/learn/06-elements#the-call-shape)).\n\n**Built-in.** An element the language provides, such as `Button` or `Card`, which the compiler knows through the registry ([Components reference](/reference)).\n\n**Case.** One value of an `enum`, written with a dot: `.primary`, `.failed(\"x\")` ([Types](/learn/12-types#enums)).\n\n**Chunk.** A page's own script and stylesheet, written to their own files and loaded the first time the page's route shows, when `build.split` is on ([Configuration](/reference/config#build)).\n\n**Component.** An element you declare, with typed props, events, slots and parts: `component UserCard(…) \{ … \}` ([Components](/learn/10-components)).\n\n**Declaration.** A top-level statement of a file: `page`, `component`, `store`, `theme`, `app`, `type`, `enum`, `api`, `const`, `data`, `image`, `animation` or `test` ([Language basics](/learn/04-language-basics#declarations)).\n\n**Derived value.** A value worked out from state and worked out again when what it reads changes: `derived total = …` ([State and reactivity](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#derived)).\n\n**Design token.** A named value that a theme sets and every built-in reads, written `$name` in a style block and `var(--name)` in a stylesheet ([Design tokens](/reference/tokens)).\n\n**Diagnostic.** A finding the compiler reports, with a code such as `T05`, a severity, a place and, where it is known, a fix; also called a *finding* ([Diagnostics](/errors)).\n\n**Effect.** Code that runs when its page shows and again when a state it read changes, with a `cleanup \{ \}` for what it set up ([State and reactivity](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#effect)).\n\n**Element.** Anything a page draws by a capitalised name — a built-in such as `Button`, or a component of your own ([Elements](/learn/06-elements)).\n\n**Enum.** A type with a fixed set of cases, declared `enum Tone \{ calm, loud \}` ([Types](/learn/12-types#enums)).\n\n**Event.** Something that happens — a click, a key, or an event a component declares and fires with `emit` — that a handler answers ([Events](/learn/08-events)).\n\n**Flag.** A word after a dot that sets a `Bool` prop or picks an enum case: `Button(\"Save\").primary.lg` ([Elements](/learn/06-elements#props-cases-and-flags)).\n\n**Handler.** Code run when an event happens, written `on click \{ … \}` ([Events](/learn/08-events#handlers)).\n\n**Hydration.** The script taking over a pre-rendered page in place, without drawing it again ([Static sites and SPAs](/about/static-or-single-page#hydration)).\n\n**Imperative block.** The body of an action, handler or effect, made of statements that do things; the opposite of a render block ([Language basics](/learn/04-language-basics#bodies)).\n\n**Layout.** A component a page names with `layout:` to frame it, which draws the page in its default slot ([Pages and routing](/learn/05-pages-and-routing#layouts)).\n\n**Lint.** A rule the compiler checks beyond whether the program can work, such as an accessibility rule or an unused-value rule; the `lints` setting changes what any finding counts as ([Configuration](/reference/config#lints)).\n\n**Page.** A declaration with a `path:` that the router draws when the address matches it: `page Home(path: \"/\") \{ … \}` ([Pages and routing](/learn/05-pages-and-routing#declaring-a-page)).\n\n**Part.** A sub-element called under its owner's name: `Card.Header`, `Panel.Footer` ([Components](/learn/10-components#parts)).\n\n**Persist.** A state kept in the browser's storage across visits: `persist scheme = \"light\"` ([Stores](/learn/11-stores#keeping-a-value-across-visits)).\n\n**Positional argument.** The one value an element takes without a name, such as a button's label or a heading's text ([Elements](/learn/06-elements#the-call-shape)).\n\n**Pre-rendered page.** The HTML the build writes for a page from everything it can know at build time, shown before any script runs; also called the *static paint* ([Static sites and SPAs](/about/static-or-single-page#what-the-static-paint-knows)).\n\n**Project script.** A `.js` file under `src/`: a plain browser script, linked on every page as written, whose top-level names `.wf` code calls directly ([JavaScript interop](/recipes/call-your-own-script)).\n\n**Prop.** A value a component or built-in takes, passed by name — or, for the one marked `_`, by position ([Components](/learn/10-components#props)).\n\n**Registry.** The compiler's table of every built-in's props, cases, flags, events, slots and parts, which the checker, the linters, the editor and the reference all read; `wf registry --json` prints it ([Command line](/reference/cli)).\n\n**Render block.** The body of a page, component or element, which describes what to show and the state behind it ([Language basics](/learn/04-language-basics#bodies)).\n\n**Resource.** A request a page makes, whose loading, error and ready states a `match` shows: `resource rows = fetch(…)` ([Fetching data](/learn/15-data#show-a-request-with-resource)).\n\n**Route parameter.** A `:name` segment of a page's path, which the page declares as a typed parameter: `page User(path: \"/user/:id\", id: String)` ([Pages and routing](/learn/05-pages-and-routing#route-parameters)).\n\n**Runtime.** The JavaScript at the head of `app.js` that the compiled pages call, reachable as `window.WF` ([Runtime API](/reference/runtime)).\n\n**Scope.** What owns the effects, timers and connections created inside it — a page, a branch, a list item — and disposes of them when it leaves ([State and reactivity](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#automatic-clean-up)).\n\n**Signal.** A reactive value, which is what a `state` is underneath: whatever reads it updates when it changes ([Runtime API](/reference/runtime#state)).\n\n**Single-page app (SPA).** A build with one HTML shell, whose pages the script swaps without a reload ([Static sites and SPAs](/about/static-or-single-page#two-shapes-of-build)).\n\n**Slot.** A place in a component that its caller fills: the default slot (`children`), a named slot, or a scoped slot that hands values to its fill ([Components](/learn/10-components#slots)).\n\n**Snapshot.** The HTML a test drew, kept under `tests/__snapshots__/` and compared on every later run ([Testing](/learn/16-testing#snapshots)).\n\n**State.** A value of a page, component or store that the page shows and that changes: `state count = 0` ([State and reactivity](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#state)).\n\n**Static build.** A build with `build.ssg: true`, which writes a pre-rendered HTML file for every page ([Static sites and SPAs](/about/static-or-single-page#two-shapes-of-build)).\n\n**Static paint.** Another name for the pre-rendered page: the HTML the build writes for a page before any script runs ([Static sites and SPAs](/about/static-or-single-page#what-the-static-paint-knows)).\n\n**Store.** Shared state with actions, built the first time something reads it ([Stores](/learn/11-stores)).\n\n**Template engine.** WebFluent used from a server, through `wf render`, Rust or Node, to render a `.wf` template with JSON data to HTML or PDF ([Server rendering](/recipes)).\n\n**Theme.** A `theme` declaration: the design tokens it changes from the baseline ([Styling](/learn/13-styling)).\n\n**Type.** A record declared with `type`, or any of the types a value can have, which the checker holds every use to ([Types](/learn/12-types)).\n\n**Validate block.** A `validate x \{ … \}` block beside a state, whose rules the control bound to that state shows ([Forms](/learn/14-forms#validate-a-field)).\n\n**`.wfx`.** A source file whose blocks are written by indentation instead of braces ([Language basics](/learn/04-language-basics#two-layouts-wf-and-wfx)).")
    }
}
